      "writtenOn": "2025-12-01T15:46:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the retry will delay expected \u0027NoNodeError\u0027. I tried to handle this case higher up the function call here: https://review.opendev.org/c/zuul/zuul/+/950862, but retrying was not an option either because of the inconsistent state of the service. Perhaps we should terminate the process when the exit handler fails because of such exception?",
      "revId": "d1648fd0a7ae8f9cd31b7fae9da117afb691ab56",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "431c82cd_0ce5a46d",
        "filename": "zuul/zk/components.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 7186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-01T16:00:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I read the documentation of kazoo.retry correctly [1], the retries only apply when the following exceptions occur: ConnectionLoss, OperationTimeout, or ForceRetryError. So a NoNodeError should still be thrown on the first attempt.\n\nTo give some context, the root issue that I want to address is that if an uncaught exception is thrown during a graceful stop, the graceful stop is canceled and the component never stops. This causes issues during pod rollouts in kubernetes, for example.\n\nSo the approach here isn\u0027t desirable, would it be okay to instead catch all exceptions in the graceful() function, log them and continue until shutdown?\n\n[1] https://kazoo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/retry.html#kazoo.retry.KazooRetry.__call__",
      "parentUuid": "3f3845f2_7c8af021",
      "revId": "d1648fd0a7ae8f9cd31b7fae9da117afb691ab56",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34a7c5f4_6e499b41",
        "filename": "zuul/zk/components.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 9311
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-09T08:17:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I see, then that sounds like a good idea. However, we shouldn\u0027t swallow the retry exceptions because the caller probably needs to know when the update fails. I think we should replace the `return` by `raise`.",
      "parentUuid": "431c82cd_0ce5a46d",
      "revId": "d1648fd0a7ae8f9cd31b7fae9da117afb691ab56",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc09f1a0_9cff1e02",
        "filename": "zuul/zk/components.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 9311
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-09T08:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the existing exception handlers, it doesn\u0027t seem like \"ConnectionLoss\" or \"OperationTimeout\" are ever expected, so it should be fine to re-throw the new exceptions.\n\nAlso, in other spots, Zuul handles the InterruptedError exception when using KazooRetry, isn\u0027t this something that we should do here?",
      "parentUuid": "34a7c5f4_6e499b41",
      "revId": "d1648fd0a7ae8f9cd31b7fae9da117afb691ab56",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca4b35fd_d6b7fad0",
        "filename": "zuul/zk/components.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 7186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-09T09:51:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Keep in mind that the original intent is to prevent the graceful stop process from being interrupted by uncaught exceptions. If we raise, then we will need to catch all exceptions at a higher level anyway (which is a good thing, I\u0027ll work on it in the next patchset amend).\n\nConnectionLoss could happen if the zookeeper node Zuul is connected to is stopped (the load balancing of zk servers always happens in the client). This may happen during a rolling update of the zookeeper ensemble. Same for OperationTimeout. You shouldn\u0027t expect the zuul executor to \"know\" it\u0027s safe to gracefully shutdown because the zookeeper ensemble is stable.\n\nThe InterruptedError is thrown when the retry is interrupted by a call to the \"interrupt\" param of the KazooRetry (None here). Since there\u0027s nothing to interrupt, such an exception will never be thrown.",
      "parentUuid": "bc09f1a0_9cff1e02",
      "revId": "d1648fd0a7ae8f9cd31b7fae9da117afb691ab56",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    }
